F Covering                | AppearanceSpecification.h | 31-37   | -                                  | ✔️ | Constructs a fully covering ink from a packed 0xRRGGBB literal.
    in    Packed  std::uint32_t          [-]  ?
    out   -       constexpr InkOrdinate  [-]  ?
    by    Api/VisibilityRaster.h, Source/VisibilityRaster.cpp

F Partial                 | AppearanceSpecification.h | 43-48   | -                                  | ✔️ | Constructs an ink at a declared coverage, matching CSS `color-mix(… n%, transparent)`.
    in    Packed    std::uint32_t          [-]  0xRRGGBB
    in    Coverage  double                 [-]  zero is invisible, one is fully covering
    out   -         constexpr InkOrdinate  [-]  ?

F Faded                   | AppearanceSpecification.h | 52-56   | -                                  | ✔️ | Scales an ink's coverage without disturbing its chromaticity — what a fade interpolant drives.
    in    Standing  InkOrdinate            [-]  ?
    in    Coverage  double                 [-]  ?
    out   -         constexpr InkOrdinate  [-]  ?
