//                                                  THE RESOLVED RECORD
//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

T AppearanceSpecification | AppearanceSpecification.h | 293-298 | contract,nonallocating,nonthrowing | -  | The one record every panel reads. Resolved at bring-up and again only when the display scale changes.
    has   Ink      SurfaceInk   [-]  ?
    has   Measure  MetricScale  [-]  ?
    has   Motion   MotionScale  [-]  ?
    by    Api/DrawerSpace.h, Api/ViewportSequence.h, Source/AppearanceSpecification.cpp, Source/DrawerSpace.cpp, Source/ViewportSequence.cpp

F Resolve                 | AppearanceSpecification.h | 305     | api,nonallocating,nonthrowing      | ✔️ | Resolves the appearance against one display scale.
    in    DisplayScale  double      [-]  what the window system reports; values at or below zero resolve at one
    out   -             Appearance  [-]  every extent already multiplied; nothing downstream multiplies again
    by    Api/AtmosphereIntegrator.h, Api/AttachmentIndex.h, Api/BrushSpecification.h, Api/DecalProjection.h, Api/DescriptorIndex.h, Api/DocumentSession.h, (+89 more)

F LatticeColumns          | AppearanceSpecification.h | 312     | api,nonallocating,nonthrowing      | ✔️ | How many lattice columns the content extent admits, from the source's four breakpoints.
    in    Measure       const MetricScale&  [-]   ?
    in    ContentAlong  float               [px]  the extent the lattice is arranged inside
    out   -             Columns             [-]   two below 640 px, then three, four, and five at and above 1024 px
    by    Source/AppearanceSpecification.cpp
